1
00:00:00,933 --> 00:00:02,167
<i>Zoey, I really have to go
somewhere.</i>

2
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:03,233
<i> Thank you.</i>

3
00:00:03,567 --> 00:00:05,200
<i>You still came even though
you know this isn't real.</i>

4
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:06,367
<i> I have something to tell you.</i>

5
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:07,767
<i> Jin Ho, he's an enemy.</i>

6
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:08,800
<i> I knew it.</i>

7
00:00:08,933 --> 00:00:09,767
<i>There's really something
about that man.</i>

8
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:10,967
<i>- Jin Ho?
- Peter?</i>

9
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:12,433
<i>- Joey!
- My condolences.</i>

10
00:00:12,567 --> 00:00:13,433
<i> Why is it closed?</i>

11
00:00:13,567 --> 00:00:14,400
<i> You can't open that, Sir.</i>

12
00:00:14,533 --> 00:00:15,567
<i> Why, Sir?</i>

13
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:17,767
<i>Sorry, curiosity got
the best of me.</i>

14
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:18,733
<i> Where's your boyfriend?</i>

15
00:00:18,867 --> 00:00:19,867
<i> He told me everything.</i>

16
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,933
<i>Did he tell you
he was with a woman?</i>

17
00:00:22,067 --> 00:00:23,433
<i> Can you help me with this?</i>

18
00:00:23,567 --> 00:00:24,600
<i> Hello? Mommy is awake?</i>

19
00:00:24,733 --> 00:00:27,267
<i>People coming out of coma
are usually like that.</i>

20
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:30,933
<i>Mom, I really want to know
who did this to you.</i>

21
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:43,267
<i> [OBB]</i>

22
00:00:52,633 --> 00:00:54,367
Andrew!

23
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:59,300
Where did you go?

24
00:01:01,167 --> 00:01:04,700
I'm sorry. Please don't be
mad at me.

25
00:01:04,833 --> 00:01:07,167
Didn't you say
you'd watch mommy?

26
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:09,033
But you just left her.

27
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:10,233
You lied to me.
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

28
00:01:10,367 --> 00:01:12,567
[SCOFFS]
So did you.

29
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:14,767
You said you were leaving
to talk to someone.

30
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:17,133
But it turns out
you just went to Joey.

31
00:01:17,267 --> 00:01:19,600
If I hadn't followed you,
I wouldn't have known.

32
00:01:19,733 --> 00:01:22,033
So, what if I went to see her?

33
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,100
I didn't lie to you.

34
00:01:24,233 --> 00:01:26,267
You didn't tell me
the truth either!

35
00:01:27,333 --> 00:01:29,567
Okay, look.

36
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:30,833
I'm sorry.

37
00:01:30,967 --> 00:01:32,633
I'm sorry I left,

38
00:01:32,767 --> 00:01:34,133
that I left your mommy.

39
00:01:34,267 --> 00:01:36,300
I didn't know
she would wake up, okay?

40
00:01:36,433 --> 00:01:39,133
And the nurse said
nothing bad happened to her.

41
00:01:39,267 --> 00:01:41,033
That's even good news, right?

42
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:43,100
That's not the point.

43
00:01:43,233 --> 00:01:45,267
You still left her.

44
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:47,400
That's how you are...

45
00:01:47,533 --> 00:01:48,933
You leave.

46
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:50,500
[SCOFFS]

47
00:01:50,633 --> 00:01:52,300
Andrew, come on.

48
00:01:52,700 --> 00:01:55,267
Really? Are you serious?
Ah, I'm trying to...

49
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:57,133
You know what? Stop that.

50
00:01:58,333 --> 00:02:01,267
Just leave, Zoey.

51
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:05,400
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

52
00:02:18,733 --> 00:02:22,800
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

53
00:02:39,767 --> 00:02:41,200
[GASPS]

54
00:02:41,333 --> 00:02:44,367
Dad, you startled me.

55
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:46,400
What are you doing here?
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

56
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:49,967
Mom sent you food.

57
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:52,033
She thought you might be hungry.

58
00:02:52,167 --> 00:02:54,633
Your mother loves me so much.

59
00:02:54,767 --> 00:02:56,700
But you shouldn't have bothered.

60
00:02:56,833 --> 00:02:59,033
There's food here.

61
00:02:59,167 --> 00:03:03,667
And it's bad to bring food
from a wake.

62
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:06,100
Fake wake, Dad.

63
00:03:06,233 --> 00:03:09,033
And there were so many visitors.

64
00:03:09,167 --> 00:03:10,600
They brought food.

65
00:03:10,733 --> 00:03:12,633
It would be a waste, right?

66
00:03:14,767 --> 00:03:16,100
Rice cake?

67
00:03:16,233 --> 00:03:17,967
This is delicious.

68
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:19,100
Okay, I'll eat this.

69
00:03:19,233 --> 00:03:21,433
- Thank you very much.
- Enjoy, Dad.

70
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:24,467
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

71
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:27,333
[PHONE RINGING]

72
00:03:36,533 --> 00:03:37,800
Hello, Andrew?

73
00:03:37,933 --> 00:03:39,300
Joey...

74
00:03:40,467 --> 00:03:42,400
Are you okay?
Is there a problem?

75
00:03:43,133 --> 00:03:45,033
None.
[DREAMY MUSIC PLAYING]

76
00:03:45,167 --> 00:03:49,067
I just had no one to share
the good news with.

77
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:50,433
Good news?

78
00:03:51,533 --> 00:03:53,067
Is that really good news?

79
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:55,533
Because your voice sounds sad.

80
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:57,400
Well, mommy woke up...

81
00:03:58,267 --> 00:04:00,100
but I still can't talk to her.

82
00:04:00,967 --> 00:04:02,567
I'm still worried.

83
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:07,133
But there's progress
in her recovery, right?

84
00:04:07,433 --> 00:04:09,833
So, don't lose hope.

85
00:04:09,967 --> 00:04:11,567
She will recover.

86
00:04:12,567 --> 00:04:14,067
<i> Never say die.</i>

87
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:15,900
Right.

88
00:04:16,133 --> 00:04:17,367
Never say die.

89
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:20,933
And I'll include your mommy
in my prayers,

90
00:04:21,067 --> 00:04:23,467
for a faster recovery.

91
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:25,433
<i> So, just hang in there.</i>

92
00:04:27,133 --> 00:04:28,467
Thank you, Joey.

93
00:04:30,133 --> 00:04:32,167
At least the one
I'm talking with...

94
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:35,033
is my partner in crime.

95
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:37,833
Zoey?

96
00:04:37,967 --> 00:04:39,333
It's you.

97
00:04:39,467 --> 00:04:42,733
[DREAMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

98
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:51,400
I was inches away
from confirming

99
00:04:51,533 --> 00:04:55,067
if that was really
Delgado's body at the wake.

100
00:04:55,467 --> 00:04:57,967
I could send one of our men
there, Berdugo.

101
00:04:58,233 --> 00:04:59,100
Do it.

102
00:04:59,233 --> 00:05:01,033
Send me proof

103
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:04,233
so I won't wonder
if what you saw was real.

104
00:05:04,367 --> 00:05:05,733
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

105
00:05:05,867 --> 00:05:07,767
I don't want problems for now.

106
00:05:07,900 --> 00:05:10,033
I'll handle it, Berdugo.

107
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:15,967
[PHONE RINGING]

108
00:05:18,167 --> 00:05:19,367
Yes, Hon.

109
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:20,867
I'll be home in a bit.

110
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,033
Hon, I'm not home yet.

111
00:05:23,267 --> 00:05:24,133
<i> Why?</i>

112
00:05:24,267 --> 00:05:25,300
Where are you?

113
00:05:25,433 --> 00:05:27,633
<i> I'm still at the hospital.</i>

114
00:05:27,767 --> 00:05:29,500
Mommy woke up.

115
00:05:30,733 --> 00:05:32,200
Really?

116
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:34,000
Did you talk to her?

117
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:35,633
Not yet.

118
00:05:35,767 --> 00:05:38,167
<i> But the doctor has high hopes</i>

119
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:42,533
that soon mommy will speak.

120
00:05:42,667 --> 00:05:44,433
That's good to hear.

121
00:05:44,567 --> 00:05:45,833
I'll go there.

122
00:05:45,967 --> 00:05:48,000
No, no need.

123
00:05:48,133 --> 00:05:49,833
I'm about to go home anyway.

124
00:05:49,967 --> 00:05:53,933
Let's just visit mommy tomorrow.

125
00:05:54,067 --> 00:05:59,100
<i>Andrew insisted he'll stay
with her tonight.</i>

126
00:05:59,233 --> 00:06:02,500
<i>I'm just so happy mommy
woke up, Tomas.</i>

127
00:06:02,633 --> 00:06:03,833
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

128
00:06:03,967 --> 00:06:05,667
Me too.

129
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:07,033
All right.

130
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:08,500
I'll go home in a bit.

131
00:06:08,633 --> 00:06:09,800
<i> Let's meet at home.</i>

132
00:06:09,933 --> 00:06:11,000
Take care.

133
00:06:11,133 --> 00:06:12,467
Okay, bye.

134
00:06:14,067 --> 00:06:16,233
Why did that old woman wake up?

135
00:06:17,067 --> 00:06:19,533
Even if she can't talk yet,

136
00:06:19,667 --> 00:06:21,867
sooner or later, she will.

137
00:06:23,767 --> 00:06:29,133
Berdugo, you've faced bigger
problems than that.

138
00:06:29,267 --> 00:06:30,533
Observe first.

139
00:06:30,667 --> 00:06:33,433
Well, worse comes to worst,

140
00:06:33,567 --> 00:06:35,767
I'll have to silence
Rebecca too.

141
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:38,233
So, finish your issue
with Delgado.

142
00:06:38,367 --> 00:06:42,467
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

143
00:06:45,033 --> 00:06:48,200
We want to thank everyone
who came here...

144
00:06:50,033 --> 00:06:52,300
and those who sympathized
with our family.

145
00:06:52,433 --> 00:06:53,900
Thank you.

146
00:06:54,567 --> 00:06:57,700
[CAMERA SHUTTER SNAPPING]

147
00:07:02,300 --> 00:07:05,600
Major Miguel Delgado was
a skilled and honest policeman.

148
00:07:05,733 --> 00:07:07,767
He was the type of policeman
who will do everything

149
00:07:07,900 --> 00:07:09,533
for service.
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

150
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:12,567
And his family has decided that,

151
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:14,900
even though it's painful
for them,

152
00:07:15,067 --> 00:07:18,167
they want everyone
to see Major Delgado...

153
00:07:19,467 --> 00:07:21,300
one last time.

154
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:26,400
[CAMERA SHUTTER SNAPPING]

155
00:07:27,867 --> 00:07:31,200
[CROWD BUZZING]

156
00:07:31,333 --> 00:07:35,233
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

157
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:41,833
[CROWD BUZZING]

158
00:07:41,967 --> 00:07:45,600
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

159
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:52,600
[PHONE RINGING]

160
00:07:53,967 --> 00:07:55,333
Boss Matias...

161
00:07:56,267 --> 00:07:57,933
There really is a body
in the coffin.

162
00:07:58,067 --> 00:07:59,133
<i> A burnt person.</i>

163
00:07:59,267 --> 00:08:00,367
Are you sure?

164
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:01,700
Yes, Boss.

165
00:08:01,833 --> 00:08:03,333
Send evidence.

166
00:08:03,467 --> 00:08:05,133
Berdugo needs it.

167
00:08:05,267 --> 00:08:06,700
Okay, Boss.

168
00:08:07,633 --> 00:08:10,400
[PHONE CHIMING]

169
00:08:10,533 --> 00:08:13,900
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

170
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:19,433
I think that's enough.
You can close it now, please.

171
00:08:19,567 --> 00:08:22,333
- [CROWD BUZZING]
- [CAMERA SHUTTER SNAPPING]

172
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:25,600
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

173
00:08:34,233 --> 00:08:35,867
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

174
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,133
The one who did this to you
will pay, Dad.

175
00:08:40,233 --> 00:08:42,500
You looked bothered
for a while now.

176
00:08:42,633 --> 00:08:44,000
Are you okay?

177
00:08:44,133 --> 00:08:46,100
I am.

178
00:08:46,233 --> 00:08:49,000
I'm just thinking
about your mommy's condition.

179
00:08:49,133 --> 00:08:51,267
I just hope
she's doing better today.

180
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:52,933
Me too.

181
00:08:53,067 --> 00:08:54,267
So, let's hurry.

182
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:56,433
I cannot wait to see mommy.

183
00:08:57,967 --> 00:08:59,267
[PHONE CHIMES]

184
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:03,533
[PHONE CHIMES]
Wait, wait, what's this?

185
00:09:04,333 --> 00:09:05,500
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

186
00:09:05,633 --> 00:09:09,167
[PHONE RINGING]

187
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:12,533
Boss, did you receive it?

188
00:09:12,667 --> 00:09:13,767
<i> Yes.</i>

189
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:16,000
That person
is not my problem anymore.

190
00:09:16,133 --> 00:09:20,433
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

191
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:23,933
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

192
00:09:24,067 --> 00:09:25,600
Hon...

193
00:09:26,467 --> 00:09:27,500
What happened?

194
00:09:27,667 --> 00:09:29,067
Nothing.

195
00:09:29,767 --> 00:09:32,500
Nothing? But your aura changed.

196
00:09:32,633 --> 00:09:34,867
You're smiling now.

197
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:36,900
You look happy.

198
00:09:37,033 --> 00:09:38,300
I am.

199
00:09:38,433 --> 00:09:40,200
You know what?

200
00:09:40,333 --> 00:09:42,267
Let's go out for dinner tonight.

201
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:44,733
I'm suddenly in the mood
for barbeque.

202
00:09:46,833 --> 00:09:49,067
Come on, let's go see your mom.

203
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:54,133
Your child is really good
at acting, Uncle Miguel.

204
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:57,400
Hey, I wasn't acting earlier.

205
00:09:58,200 --> 00:10:00,700
Actually, I really cried
because I thought,

206
00:10:00,833 --> 00:10:02,400
what if that was really you,
Dad?

207
00:10:02,567 --> 00:10:04,033
I won't be able handle it.

208
00:10:04,167 --> 00:10:05,533
Me too.

209
00:10:05,667 --> 00:10:09,100
Maybe I wouldn't believe it
or hope you'd get up again,

210
00:10:09,233 --> 00:10:11,467
like you did now.

211
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:14,867
Well, even I got scared
of being separated from you.

212
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,733
But let's not think about that.

213
00:10:16,867 --> 00:10:18,900
It's still far from happening.

214
00:10:19,967 --> 00:10:22,733
Now, maybe no one will suspect
that I'm still alive.

215
00:10:22,867 --> 00:10:24,300
Let's not be too sure.

216
00:10:24,433 --> 00:10:25,767
It's better to be safe.

217
00:10:25,900 --> 00:10:27,500
Major Delgado...

218
00:10:27,633 --> 00:10:29,367
I know you're eager,

219
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:31,167
but stay here for the meantime.
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

220
00:10:31,300 --> 00:10:33,567
We didn't stage this wake

221
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:36,433
just for the syndicate
to catch you later.

222
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:38,133
Do I make myself clear?

223
00:10:38,267 --> 00:10:39,867
Yes, Sir.

224
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,900
Just update me about Berdugo.

225
00:10:44,633 --> 00:10:48,600
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

226
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:07,967
Where are we really going?

227
00:11:08,133 --> 00:11:10,233
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING♪]

228
00:11:10,367 --> 00:11:11,967
Hey.

229
00:11:13,333 --> 00:11:15,200
You said you got close
to Jin Ho

230
00:11:15,333 --> 00:11:17,333
when we went to Valmora, right?

231
00:11:17,467 --> 00:11:18,933
Yes, why?

232
00:11:19,067 --> 00:11:20,533
Because I've been
texting him, look.

233
00:11:20,667 --> 00:11:22,433
He's not replying.

234
00:11:22,667 --> 00:11:23,967
He just read it.

235
00:11:24,967 --> 00:11:26,667
Maybe he's hiding now.

236
00:11:26,800 --> 00:11:29,167
Remember, the police were
looking for him last time.

237
00:11:29,300 --> 00:11:30,633
Exactly, that's why
I'm asking you,

238
00:11:30,767 --> 00:11:34,333
maybe you know
where we can find him.

239
00:11:34,467 --> 00:11:36,100
Why? Are you going
to have him arrested?

240
00:11:36,233 --> 00:11:37,467
No.

241
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:38,500
I just want to make sure

242
00:11:38,633 --> 00:11:40,867
he still trusts us.

243
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:41,967
Of course, this is our chance

244
00:11:42,133 --> 00:11:44,600
to see those syndicates.

245
00:11:45,567 --> 00:11:47,533
So, Peter, please help me.

246
00:11:47,667 --> 00:11:50,700
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES♪]

247
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:54,433
Wow...

248
00:11:54,567 --> 00:11:57,400
This new branch of the gym
is impressive.

249
00:11:57,533 --> 00:12:00,067
Has it crossed your mind that
maybe they closed the old one

250
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:03,367
because they are hiding,
or they're hiding Jin Ho?

251
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:05,567
Come on!
If they were really hiding,

252
00:12:05,933 --> 00:12:07,233
why would they post the address
of the new branch

253
00:12:07,367 --> 00:12:09,200
at the old gym?

254
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:11,967
- Right?
- True.

255
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:13,800
Sorry, I'm just paranoid.

256
00:12:14,667 --> 00:12:15,767
Okay, here's the deal.

257
00:12:15,900 --> 00:12:18,000
The only reason I agreed
to come with you

258
00:12:18,133 --> 00:12:20,267
is so we can see
if Jin Ho is really here

259
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:24,633
and prove if he's part
of the syndicate.

260
00:12:24,767 --> 00:12:27,867
And we should make him admit
why he went with Liza.

261
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:31,533
Well, I know you won't betray
your oppa.

262
00:12:32,533 --> 00:12:34,967
Of course, we're close.

263
00:12:35,100 --> 00:12:36,067
We're bros.
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

264
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:38,733
I also want to hear his side.

265
00:12:38,867 --> 00:12:39,867
But, wait.

266
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,600
What do you even do
in a boxing gym?

267
00:12:42,733 --> 00:12:46,800
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

268
00:12:49,467 --> 00:12:52,167
[CHUCKLES]
<i> Oppa.</i>

269
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:53,533
What else?

270
00:12:53,667 --> 00:12:55,867
Workouts, sparring.

271
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,800
Wow, do you even know how?

272
00:12:57,933 --> 00:12:59,033
Wow, the way you ask me,

273
00:12:59,167 --> 00:13:01,333
it's like you don't believe
in me.

274
00:13:01,467 --> 00:13:03,167
I do, just a little.

275
00:13:03,300 --> 00:13:05,500
You have no idea,
I'm tough in the ring.

276
00:13:05,633 --> 00:13:07,567
I've been learning
a lot of moves now.

277
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:09,900
- Really?
- I learned from my idol!

278
00:13:10,033 --> 00:13:10,967
Idol?

279
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:13,300
Yes, Eman Bacosa Pacquiao!

280
00:13:13,433 --> 00:13:15,300
- He's my idol!
- Oh, he's my idol too!

281
00:13:15,433 --> 00:13:17,033
He's my dad's idol too!
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

282
00:13:17,167 --> 00:13:18,833
I watched his last fight.

283
00:13:18,967 --> 00:13:20,033
- He had five knockouts.
- And?

284
00:13:20,167 --> 00:13:22,633
Then after the knockout,
he even did a flying kiss.

285
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:25,133
And Jillian Ward
was even there watching!

286
00:13:25,267 --> 00:13:26,167
They say I look like her.

287
00:13:26,300 --> 00:13:27,400
Yes, I have a crush on her.

288
00:13:27,533 --> 00:13:30,133
- Really?
- She's lucky, so cool.

289
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:31,267
You know what, let's go.

290
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:32,633
Let's find Jin Ho.

291
00:13:32,767 --> 00:13:36,000
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

292
00:13:40,533 --> 00:13:41,933
They're sparring, look.

293
00:13:42,967 --> 00:13:47,733
- [THUDDING]
- [SUAVE MUSIC PLAYING]

294
00:13:47,867 --> 00:13:49,267
Come on, let's watch this first.

295
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:52,133
[THUDDING]

296
00:13:54,233 --> 00:13:57,533
[THUDDING]

297
00:13:57,700 --> 00:13:59,767
That one,
his moves are so clean.

298
00:14:00,533 --> 00:14:03,067
[THUDDING]

299
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:04,933
[SUAVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

300
00:14:05,067 --> 00:14:06,967
That's exactly what Jin Ho
and I did

301
00:14:07,100 --> 00:14:08,667
when we trained before.

302
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:10,067
There, look.

303
00:14:10,200 --> 00:14:11,833
<i> Jab, jab, jab, let's go.</i>

304
00:14:11,967 --> 00:14:13,367
- There, look.
- So good!

305
00:14:13,500 --> 00:14:14,733
Good, right?

306
00:14:14,867 --> 00:14:16,333
He's really good!

307
00:14:16,467 --> 00:14:18,933
[THUDDING]

308
00:14:20,567 --> 00:14:22,867
He's fast, look!
And look at his footwork.

309
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:24,433
And his power, look, look.

310
00:14:24,567 --> 00:14:26,167
[CHUCKLES]

311
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:27,900
Amazing!

312
00:14:29,033 --> 00:14:31,400
[BUZZER BLARES]

313
00:14:31,533 --> 00:14:32,767
<i> Break!</i>

314
00:14:36,733 --> 00:14:40,733
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

315
00:14:41,733 --> 00:14:43,900
- Eman!
- Eman!

316
00:14:44,033 --> 00:14:48,100
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

317
00:14:57,667 --> 00:15:01,633
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

318
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:09,267
Oh my gosh!

319
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:10,800
Really? That's you?

320
00:15:10,933 --> 00:15:12,100
Idol, I watched your fight!

321
00:15:12,233 --> 00:15:13,200
You were amazing!

322
00:15:13,333 --> 00:15:14,633
- Thank you, thank you.
- Idol.

323
00:15:14,767 --> 00:15:15,567
Hello.

324
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:17,000
Boss, I'll just go
to the restroom, okay?

325
00:15:17,867 --> 00:15:18,967
I watched your fight.

326
00:15:19,100 --> 00:15:20,600
You knocked out your opponent
five times!

327
00:15:20,733 --> 00:15:22,600
- Incredible! You're so strong!
- Yes!

328
00:15:22,733 --> 00:15:23,800
Can we take a picture?

329
00:15:23,933 --> 00:15:26,400
[SUAVE MUSIC PLAYING]

330
00:15:26,533 --> 00:15:27,733
[CROWD CLAMORING]

331
00:15:27,867 --> 00:15:29,733
Hey, wait, let me get one first!

332
00:15:29,867 --> 00:15:31,733
Wow, that's a crowd!

333
00:15:31,867 --> 00:15:35,867
[CLAMORING CONTINUES]

334
00:15:36,033 --> 00:15:39,767
[SUAVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

335
00:15:41,700 --> 00:15:44,300
Come on, let's go, we're still
looking for Jim Ho.

336
00:15:44,433 --> 00:15:48,467
[SUAVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

337
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:56,733
[LIFE MONITOR BEEPING]

338
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:03,767
Mom?

339
00:16:03,900 --> 00:16:05,767
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

340
00:16:05,900 --> 00:16:07,133
Mom...

341
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:09,533
Good morning, Mom.

342
00:16:14,900 --> 00:16:16,733
Can you see me?

343
00:16:19,767 --> 00:16:21,400
Sis, mommy is awake.

344
00:16:22,667 --> 00:16:24,000
She opened her eyes.

345
00:16:25,433 --> 00:16:26,600
Mom...

346
00:16:27,867 --> 00:16:30,100
Hi, Mom. How's your sleep?

347
00:16:32,033 --> 00:16:34,200
We're here for you.

348
00:16:34,333 --> 00:16:35,667
We're right here.

349
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:39,367
And you have another visitor.

350
00:16:39,500 --> 00:16:42,533
He brought something
special for you.

351
00:16:45,533 --> 00:16:49,567
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

352
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:56,167
Hi, Mom.

353
00:16:56,300 --> 00:17:00,567
[LIFE MONITOR BEEPING RAPIDLY]

354
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:04,633
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

355
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:07,333
Mom?

356
00:17:07,467 --> 00:17:10,800
[LIFE MONITOR BEEPING RAPIDLY]

357
00:17:11,767 --> 00:17:13,467
Sis, what's happening to mommy?

358
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:14,900
Mom?

359
00:17:16,333 --> 00:17:17,200
Nurse...

360
00:17:17,333 --> 00:17:19,433
Can you please come here
and check my mom?

361
00:17:20,833 --> 00:17:22,167
Mommy, please relax.

362
00:17:22,300 --> 00:17:23,567
[REBECCA GRUNTS]
Mommy...

363
00:17:23,700 --> 00:17:25,800
Mom, relax, we're right here.

364
00:17:25,933 --> 00:17:28,333
[REBECCA GRUNTING]
What's it, Mom?

365
00:17:28,467 --> 00:17:31,333
[REBECCA GRUNTING]

366
00:17:32,900 --> 00:17:34,633
Maybe she's having
a heart attack?

367
00:17:34,767 --> 00:17:36,667
Honey, look, look.

368
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:39,367
Look at her,
look at her finger.

369
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:41,567
It's like mommy wants to say
something, Sis.

370
00:17:41,700 --> 00:17:43,267
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

371
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:45,067
[GRUNTS]

372
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,067
Doc, can you please
check my mom?

373
00:17:52,333 --> 00:17:55,000
[GRUNTING]

374
00:17:57,500 --> 00:18:00,667
That's Eun Ji,
the owner of this gym.

375
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:02,533
Jin Ho introduced him to me
before,

376
00:18:02,667 --> 00:18:05,900
and he said they were friends
back in Korea.

377
00:18:06,033 --> 00:18:08,633
So, maybe he knows
where Jin Ho is now.

378
00:18:10,333 --> 00:18:12,267
Hopefully he answers us.

379
00:18:15,133 --> 00:18:16,033
Miss?

380
00:18:16,467 --> 00:18:18,233
Do you still remember me?

381
00:18:18,367 --> 00:18:22,033
I was with your boss's
best friend, Jin Ho.

382
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:24,067
We trained at your old branch.

383
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:25,133
Do you remember?

384
00:18:25,267 --> 00:18:26,300
Yes, Sir!

385
00:18:26,433 --> 00:18:27,900
Are you going to train again?

386
00:18:28,033 --> 00:18:31,900
But Sir Jin Ho hasn't come back
here for a long time.

387
00:18:32,133 --> 00:18:34,467
What about his friend,
the owner?

388
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:36,567
- Eun Ji.
- Ah, Sir Eun Ji?

389
00:18:36,700 --> 00:18:38,467
Where is he?
[SPEAKS IN KOREAN]

390
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:40,867
Someone's following me!
Please help me!

391
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,433
- Wait, wait!
- You're running away from us?

392
00:18:43,567 --> 00:18:45,200
- Please help me!
- Sir, calm down.

393
00:18:45,333 --> 00:18:47,700
We can talk about this.

394
00:18:47,833 --> 00:18:50,300
Little girl, don't meddle here.

395
00:18:50,433 --> 00:18:52,133
He owes us big time.

396
00:18:52,267 --> 00:18:55,267
So, we'll do whatever we want.

397
00:18:55,433 --> 00:18:57,833
If you have a problem,
don't resort to violence.

398
00:19:01,667 --> 00:19:02,900
<i> Do you want to get hurt too?</i>

399
00:19:03,033 --> 00:19:04,000
Hey...

400
00:19:04,133 --> 00:19:06,300
don't hurt Joey.

401
00:19:06,433 --> 00:19:08,167
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

402
00:19:08,300 --> 00:19:10,500
Peter! Stop that!

403
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:13,267
You're meddling?

404
00:19:14,167 --> 00:19:15,433
[GRUNTS]

405
00:19:15,567 --> 00:19:17,133
You're fighting back?

406
00:19:17,267 --> 00:19:20,133
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

407
00:19:20,267 --> 00:19:21,800
Boss, she's a woman.

408
00:19:23,933 --> 00:19:25,567
- [REBECCA WHIMPERING]
- [LIFE MONITOR BEEPING]

409
00:19:25,700 --> 00:19:27,267
Mom...
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

410
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:29,367
[REBECCA WHIMPERING]

411
00:19:31,167 --> 00:19:33,500
[WHIMPERING]

412
00:19:33,633 --> 00:19:37,033
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

413
00:19:38,400 --> 00:19:40,833
<i> Let's let her rest for now.</i>

414
00:19:40,967 --> 00:19:42,500
Let's just talk outside.

415
00:19:44,367 --> 00:19:46,033
Mommy?

416
00:19:46,467 --> 00:19:47,633
Wait, okay?

417
00:19:47,767 --> 00:19:52,267
- [LIFE MONITOR BEEPING]
- [FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

418
00:20:01,300 --> 00:20:04,833
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

419
00:20:07,100 --> 00:20:08,267
Put him to sleep, quickly!
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

420
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:09,933
Not possible, I'm a boxer.

421
00:20:10,067 --> 00:20:12,367
Ah, you're the boxer.

422
00:20:12,500 --> 00:20:15,200
Do you want to end up
like his last opponent?

423
00:20:15,333 --> 00:20:17,200
That guy got knocked down
five times.

424
00:20:17,433 --> 00:20:18,333
Knockdown?

425
00:20:18,467 --> 00:20:19,833
You're useless.

426
00:20:19,967 --> 00:20:21,633
You pretend you're defending
the woman,

427
00:20:21,767 --> 00:20:24,833
but in truth, you're nothing!

428
00:20:24,967 --> 00:20:26,633
[GRUNTING]

429
00:20:26,767 --> 00:20:28,700
- [THUDDING]
- [GROANING]

430
00:20:29,700 --> 00:20:31,000
- [THUDS]
- [GROANS]

431
00:20:32,300 --> 00:20:33,967
I thought you said
it wasn't possible?

432
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:36,333
Of course, I'll defend you.

433
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:37,467
Boss, Boss!
Let's get out of here, Boss!

434
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:39,067
Call the police!

435
00:20:41,500 --> 00:20:43,133
That's right, get out of here!

436
00:20:43,267 --> 00:20:44,400
And don't come back!

437
00:20:44,533 --> 00:20:45,567
You're nothing compared to Eman!

438
00:20:45,700 --> 00:20:47,200
We're not done yet!

439
00:20:47,333 --> 00:20:49,300
You will repay me!

440
00:20:49,567 --> 00:20:50,667
You will repay me!

441
00:20:50,800 --> 00:20:52,133
Leave! Now!

442
00:20:54,733 --> 00:20:55,633
Joey, are you okay?

443
00:20:55,767 --> 00:20:57,400
I'm fine.

444
00:20:57,533 --> 00:20:59,100
Are you okay?

445
00:20:59,233 --> 00:21:00,600
I'm fine too.

446
00:21:00,733 --> 00:21:02,433
Thank you, guys,
you're so kind.

447
00:21:02,567 --> 00:21:03,600
- Okay.
- You...

448
00:21:03,733 --> 00:21:05,867
You actually look familiar.

449
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,000
We're looking for you.

450
00:21:07,133 --> 00:21:09,833
We wanted to ask
about your friend Jin Ho.

451
00:21:10,133 --> 00:21:12,367
- Jin Ho?
- Where is he?

452
00:21:12,500 --> 00:21:14,100
I don't know.

453
00:21:14,233 --> 00:21:15,667
We have had no contact
for a long time.

454
00:21:15,800 --> 00:21:16,833
I can't reach him.

455
00:21:16,967 --> 00:21:19,000
Is that true?
Maybe you're just hiding him.

456
00:21:19,133 --> 00:21:20,267
- Tell us!
- No!

457
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:22,300
You saved my life.
Why would I lie to you?

458
00:21:22,433 --> 00:21:23,533
Promise.

459
00:21:23,667 --> 00:21:24,933
No contact.

460
00:21:25,467 --> 00:21:27,333
Eman! They said you got
into a fight.

461
00:21:27,467 --> 00:21:28,333
Come on, let's go.

462
00:21:28,467 --> 00:21:30,067
Okay, Coach.
Take care, okay?

463
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:31,000
- Let's go!
- Bye!

464
00:21:31,133 --> 00:21:32,300
Thank you!

465
00:21:32,433 --> 00:21:36,433
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

466
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,900
Doc, why did mommy
react like that?

467
00:21:41,033 --> 00:21:41,933
It's like she got scared

468
00:21:42,100 --> 00:21:44,767
when my sister
and Tomas came in.

469
00:21:45,167 --> 00:21:46,900
I can't be sure.
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

470
00:21:47,033 --> 00:21:49,467
Maybe something triggered
her emotions.

471
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:52,067
Trigger?
What do you mean?

472
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:55,200
It can be a memory
or her senses.

473
00:21:55,333 --> 00:21:58,000
Something she smelled, heard,
or saw.

474
00:21:58,133 --> 00:22:01,100
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

475
00:22:02,800 --> 00:22:06,233
[LIFE MONITOR BEEPING]

476
00:22:06,367 --> 00:22:10,767
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

477
00:22:12,367 --> 00:22:14,800
Even in your condition,

478
00:22:14,933 --> 00:22:17,000
you're still fighting, Rebecca.

479
00:22:18,033 --> 00:22:20,933
Someone almost noticed
what you did.

480
00:22:25,900 --> 00:22:28,700
I know you can hear me.

481
00:22:28,833 --> 00:22:30,300
Remember...

482
00:22:30,433 --> 00:22:33,633
if you say anything
about what I did to you,

483
00:22:35,267 --> 00:22:37,800
I won't just go after you.

484
00:22:37,933 --> 00:22:40,267
I'll go after
your two children too.

485
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:43,033
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

486
00:22:43,167 --> 00:22:45,033
Do you understand me?

487
00:22:49,433 --> 00:22:53,400
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

488
00:22:56,633 --> 00:22:57,933
Good.

489
00:22:59,567 --> 00:23:02,133
I'm glad we had
this conversation.

490
00:23:02,267 --> 00:23:06,133
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

491
00:23:13,033 --> 00:23:17,033
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

492
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:21,433
Who are you looking for?

493
00:23:21,600 --> 00:23:23,233
Ah, Sir Eman.

494
00:23:23,367 --> 00:23:24,267
Oh, it's you.

495
00:23:24,400 --> 00:23:25,833
- Shall we?
- Let's go?

496
00:23:25,967 --> 00:23:28,167
I suddenly remembered
Ma'am Rebecca.

497
00:23:28,300 --> 00:23:31,233
Maybe I should visit her.

498
00:23:31,367 --> 00:23:32,333
Help me.

499
00:23:32,467 --> 00:23:34,000
Is someone trying to kill her?

500
00:23:34,133 --> 00:23:36,633
Make sure before the day ends,

501
00:23:36,767 --> 00:23:37,900
she's no longer alive!

502
00:23:38,033 --> 00:23:40,433
We already placed a tracker
in Jin Ho's car.

503
00:23:40,567 --> 00:23:41,833
Last movement recorded,

504
00:23:41,967 --> 00:23:45,333
2:17 AM at Bolivar Mushroom
Chips Manufacturing.

505
00:23:45,467 --> 00:23:48,567
Peter and I plan
to confront Jin Ho.

506
00:23:48,700 --> 00:23:50,133
Text me where you are.

507
00:23:50,267 --> 00:23:50,767
I'm on my way.

508
00:23:50,900 --> 00:23:52,433
We'll follow Jin Ho.

509
00:23:52,567 --> 00:23:55,233
I'm going to deal with
that so-called friend of his.

510
00:23:55,400 --> 00:23:56,700
- Joey!
- Jin Ho.

511
00:23:56,833 --> 00:23:59,633
I'm here. I'm just looking
for a spot where we can talk.

512
00:23:59,767 --> 00:24:00,767
Joey, wait for a while, okay?

513
00:24:00,900 --> 00:24:03,000
Andrew, what is it?
Andrew, what's happening?

514
00:24:03,133 --> 00:24:04,833
It looks like something bad
happened to him!

515
00:24:04,967 --> 00:24:06,767
Come on, let's go to him!
Hurry!
